{
	"_comment": "Request transcripts of the prediction debounce and rate floor, replayed through _shared/lua/llm/request_plan/debounce.lua by the macOS and Linux runners. A vector gives the floor in milliseconds (floor_ms, the one value the user sets, which the floor port answers) and an ordered list of steps. A step calls one method of the plan with args (plus now_ms for on_dispatch and on_sent, the caller's monotonic clock in milliseconds) and lists the decisions it returns, in order, as expect, or a substring the raised message must contain as expect_error. Tokens count from 1 per plan, one per arm. An arm decision means: cancel nothing else and start a one-shot timer of delay_ms; cancel means stop that token; fire and stale answer on_timer; send and defer answer on_dispatch. There is one behaviour for every driver, written in shared_behaviour; drivers records who replays this file. A port in another language replays it unchanged.",
	"shared_behaviour": {
		"never": "A negative debounce (the stored value -1) turns the automatic trigger off; an explicit trigger, an override request and live mode still arm.",
		"explicit_requests": "An explicit request (shortcut, typed trigger, prompt action) and the later variants of its sequential run are never held by the rate floor; only automatic requests wait.",
		"floor": "One last-request time for every backend and every kind of request; the interval is the user's llm.trigger.min_request_interval_ms.",
		"live_word_end": "A word end fires instantly in live mode too when the instant word end setting is on."
	},
	"drivers": {
		"macos": "Replays every vector (_shared/lua/test/llm_request_plan_contract.lua).",
		"linux": "Replays every vector (_shared/lua/test/llm_request_plan_contract.lua).",
		"windows": "Not ported yet: the AutoHotkey engine must reach the same shared_behaviour and replay every vector; see the report of the 2026-10-26 request floor pass for the list of changes."
	},
